      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="1298674479">
          <groundspeak:date>2025-05-15T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="25790230">MaybeSunshine</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP331 Stavely [FOUND]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On a short day trip down thisaway for a mental break from work (hmm, when have I ever said that before?) A quick find under an easily removed cover beside the most mistreated benchmark sign I’ve ever seen. Thanks!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684684014">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-07T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3061435">Iron Phoenix</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP331 - Stavely&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Out for yet another day of capping and caching with OBA, this time in Lethbridge!! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; Along the way there and back. &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_wink.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; Another odd cap that I wasn't expecting.  I wandered up and down the fence after I'd taken photos to make sure it was the only little manhole there. TFTCap!!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684657949">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-07T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="540154">One Bad Ant</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP331 - Stavely - I made Iron Phoenix leap the water in the ditch while I took the easy way (dry way). That's an interesting cap.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="681449486">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-24T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="1298988">dronnord</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP331 Stavely&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;N 50° 09.914 W 113° 38.815&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;My elevations are all toast so I will not even bother putting them here anymore today.  We pulled into Stavely As we arrived and I removed obstacles to the BCP, the locals wandered over, I gave the landowner an update on what I was doing at his fenceline and then on the drive afterward, I gave CC21 some direction on First Order Benchmarks and mean sea level elevations and how the entire system was devised and created in Canada. Poor Him !&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks for the BCP OFTH..onward..3rd of the day&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="680847802">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-22T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="1685537">nosweat6060</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP331 Stavely

I was on my way to Calgary and stopped off along the way to look for this brass cap. It was an easy find along a fence line. Thanks OFTH for this series.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
